2. DATA (the colour sample: `data/sample.json` and everything generated from it)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   You are free to share and adapt the dataset for any purpose, including
   commercially, provided you give appropriate credit.

   Attribution: "Chinese Colour Library — YIVA Digital (https://yivadigital.com/colors)"

   This repository ships a curated 33-colour sample. The full 161-colour library
   (24 solar terms x 4 roles) is published at https://yivadigital.com/colors.

   The underlying colour names and classical citations belong to public-domain
   Chinese classical texts and openly published colour references (see
   `data/sample.json` -> `meta.sources`).

3. TRADEMARK / THIRD-PARTY NOTICE
   -------------------------------
   - "Pantone" is a trademark of Pantone LLC. Pantone values in this dataset are
     NEAREST PERCEPTUAL MATCHES taken from an unofficial community dataset and are
     NOT official Pantone colour references. Verify against Pantone Connect or
     official swatches before commercial colour-critical use.
   - CSS named colours are defined by W3C and are reproduced under their terms.
   - Traditional Chinese colours have no single standard value; the HEX values are
     common reference conversions, not canonical.
